  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 213 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nFriday through Tuesday Assessment...a certainty of windy conditions \nthrough Friday with frost Friday night. The probability of a \nfreeze is at 20-30 percent.\n\nA strong cold front will sweep through the area Thursday night \nbringing windy conditions late Thursday night through mid-day \nFriday. All models show a trop fold moving through the area during \nthis time frame which will increase winds. The models generally \nagree the trop fold will be down to 400-500 mb but some solutions \nhave the trop fold as sub 500 mb. Overall, we are looking at \nsustained winds between 15-25 mph and gusts of 30-40 mph. Confidence \nis lower on the higher end of the wind gust range, but cannot be \nruled out. Headlines are not expected at this time. \n\nCold Canadian high pressure bringing the frost potential to much of \nthe area Friday night into Saturday morning. Cloud cover will be the \nkey to how cold it will get. The potential for freezing temperatures \nis also there, especially north of Highway 30. Right now the \nprobability of freezing temperatures is at 20-30 percent. Late this \nweekend and into next week, guidance continues to favor above normal \ntemperatures returning to the area, along with mostly dry\nconditions.",
